Node.js release signing keys, for checking the Node a release is built from
(.github/workflows/release.yml: gpgv on SHASUMS256.txt.sig, then sha256 of the tarball).

Source: https://github.com/nodejs/release-keys at commit
481637f813e912c4aa3622d7964ab426c97b8e8d (2026-09-01): every key in keys.list, exported
with gpg --export --armor --export-options export-minimal. Node 24.22.3's SHASUMS256.txt is
signed by 5BE8A3F6C8A5C01D106C0AD820B1A390B168D356 (checked 2026-11-23).
To update: take keys.list and keys/*.asc from that repository at a newer commit, and
re-export the same way. gpg ignores the text before the armor line.

